        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Waris Hussein, Mathieu Kassovitz\n- Roles: television director, film director, director, screenwriter, producer, editor, actor\n- Works: Doctor Who, Play of the Month, A Passage to India, Amélie, Le Fabuleux Destin d'Amélie Poulain\n\nFacts:\n- Waris Hussein was born on 9 December 1938.\n- Waris Hussein is a British-Indian television director and film director.\n- In 1965, Waris Hussein was known for British television productions including the Play of the Month version of A Passage to India.\n- Waris Hussein was also known for British television productions including Doctor Who.\n- Mathieu Kassovitz was born on 3 August 1967.\n- Mathieu Kassovitz is a French director, screenwriter, producer, editor, and actor.\n- In Francophone countries, Mathieu Kassovitz was probably best known for playing Nino Quincampoix in Amélie, released in 2001 as Le Fabuleux Destin d'Amélie Poulain.",
